content:
{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Confirm sender account, mailbox usage, and devices"
}

{
  "query": "Outlook inbox rules not working",
  "reason": "Provided articles don't cover inbox rules"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0105",
  "reason": "Confirm laptop is online and healthy, rule out client-side issues"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, sorry your Outlook rules have stopped sorting your mail. I checked a few things on our side. Your mailbox is only about 24% full and your laptop is online with no warnings, so those aren't the cause. To find the problem, could you tell me: 1) Have all of your rules stopped, or only some? If only some, which ones, and what should they do? 2) Do your rules work if you open Outlook on the web in your browser? 3) Did anything change around the time they stopped, like an update, a new laptop or Outlook profile, or new or edited rules? 4) Have you seen any error messages? Also, in Outlook go to File > Manage Rules & Alerts, and check that the rules still have their boxes ticked and that none of them say \"client-only\". Closing and reopening Outlook, or restarting your laptop, is also worth a try. Once I hear back, I'll take the next step.",
  "internal_note": "P3 email ticket: Outlook inbox rules haven't sorted mail into folders since last week. Checked: user is active (user_id 5, HR, not VIP, no lockout). Mailbox is at 24.4% of 50 GB, so quota isn't the cause (KB-010). Laptop BL-LT-0105 is online, 47% disk free, no warnings. No KB article covers inbox rules; searched the KB and found only KB-009/010/011, which don't apply. Asked the user: are all rules affected or only some, do rules run in Outlook on the web (server-side vs client-only), what changed recently, and any errors. Also asked her to check that rules are enabled and to restart Outlook. Possible causes to look at next: rules marked client-only, rules disabled or corrupted, the server-side rules size limit, a profile rebuild, or an Outlook update. If rules also fail in Outlook on the web, or the cause stays unclear, escalate to Tier 2 to review the mailbox rules from the server side. A KB article on inbox rules would help with tickets like this.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-009",
    "KB-010"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
